{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788279193,"nonce":"xpSlxfBgG/ksvtfyIzor5bILNQ0=","message":"LANDED — `122973e`, merged `e9c47ea`, rebuilt `8b804c5`. Three resolutions from\nthe implementing session, posted by the orchestrator because the worker\ncorrectly declined to write git-bug from its worktree (two identities exist and\nthe refs are shared with the main checkout — a concurrent write was the risk).\nVerified against the decompiled source before posting.\n\n**1. `buildable:true` REFUSES `mode:\"near\"`, and this issue's wording implies a\nflag that does not exist.** The body says `canWipeEdifices:true` \"stays on the\ngod-hand path only; buildable mode does not pass it.\" There is nothing to\nwithhold: `canWipeEdifices` is a parameter of `GenSpawn.CanSpawnAt`, and the\nbuildable path never calls `CanSpawnAt` at all — it calls\n`GenConstruct.CanPlaceBlueprintAt`. The real hazard is different and worse:\n`GenPlace`'s radial search under `mode:\"near\"` can land the building on a cell\nthe gate never evaluated, which is `acee526`'s whole subject. So `buildable:true`\nrefuses `near` rather than validating one cell and placing on another.\n\n**2. `dev:starter-kit` needed ONE CALL PER BUILDING UNIT, not `mode:\"direct\"` —\nand doing item 3 literally is a REGRESSION.** `dev:spawn-thing` runs a stack\nloop for `count`, so `count:2` in direct mode targets one cell twice.\n`GenSpawn.SpawningWipes(Bed, Bed)` is true for two edifices, so the second bed\n**vanishes the first** while the envelope reports `placed: 2`. `Near` mode was\nhiding this by scattering them. The `medical` preset is the live case. Fixed as\none call per unit with distinct gated cells.\n\n**3. The other two fixture routes honour the ground half and REPORT the widget\nhalf, rather than enforcing both.** `world-fixture`'s `bench` step and\n`JournalVerbs.SpawnPlayerBuilding` had **no validator at all** — not even\n`CanSpawnAt`. Adopting the full `buildable:true` semantics would delete a\nshipped fixture: `journal-selftest power` places a `PowerConduit`, which needs\nElectricity, and that step runs on fresh maps where it is not researched. So the\nplacement gate applies and the research/tech gate is reported alongside rather\nthan refused on. `dev:spawn-thing {buildable:true}` keeps both halves.\n\n**Not demonstrated.** Nothing has run against a game; the bench pass is the\norchestrator's and `wiped[]` is entirely unexercised, because nothing in the\nsession-15 pass placed onto an occupied cell. The two adopted fixture routes are\nthe early smoke call — if either now refuses, that is a shipped fixture\nbreaking, and it is the first thing to look at.","files":null}]}